  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 229 AM CDT Tue Jun 2 2026\n\nRain chances and cooler temperatures will return to the area by \nmid to late week. A mid/upper level low will develop over the Baja\nregion on Wednesday and move into northern Mexico by the end of \nthe week. Periodic disturbances ahead of this\u00a0feature will lift \nnortheast across West Texas, and\u00a0interact with a very moist \nairmass, resulting in medium to high rain chances (50 to 80%) \nWednesday through Friday. This system will lift northeast across \nWest Texas over the weekend, resulting in additional rain chances \n(30-50%) across the area. The main concern this week will be a \nthreat for heavy rainfall and some localized flash flooding, due \nto the very moist airmass. The severe threat will remain low, due \nto weak flow aloft. Temperatures will be considerably cooler for \nearly June, with highs in the 80s areawide by mid to late week. \nTemperatures warm a bit over the weekend, with highs in the upper \n80s and lower 90s by Sunday.",
